  "scope": "Retrospective diagnosis of frozen nominal v2 exploratory generated-demand simulations; sampled first-seed traces only, all twenty seeds for outcomes",
  "findings": [
    "Every modeled city control has at most three green phases, activating topology fallback instead of risk optimization.",
    "All sampled nontrivial decisions choose small_phase_pressure_fallback; risk-aware search and network objectives are never evaluated on these phase topologies.",
    "Calgary max-pressure / prototype averages 21.2641 s vs fixed18.62082 s. Original predictive MPC19.13077 s still slightly regresses fixed; topology alone does not establish out-of-distribution safety.",
    "Original MPC generally switches more yet delays less; fewer switches alone is not an improvement.",
    "Existing corridors use generated demand and unsurveyed signal timing. These comparisons diagnose simulator behavior, not field performance."
  ],
